"Husk fetches it once and mounts it whenever JIT is turned on. If that download hangs, get the files here instead: download them from this screen, or import them from Files." = "Husk 只会下载它一次，之后每次开启 JIT 都会直接挂载。如果下载卡住了，可以在这里自己取文件：在本次页面下载，或从“文件”导入。";

"Husk needs memory it can write and then execute, which on iOS takes an attached debugger." = "Husk 需要既可写又可执行的内存，在 iOS 上这需要附加调试器。";

"Husk needs memory it can write and then execute, which on iOS takes an attached debugger. There are two ways to get it: a debugger that services trap requests, or a MAP_JIT mapping, which the kernel allows any debugged process. Either one is enough — which is available depends on the device and the iOS version, so Husk tests both rather than assuming." = "Husk 需要既可写又可执行的内存，在 iOS 上这需要附加一个调试器。有两种途径：一种是为陷阱请求提供服务的调试器，另一种是 MAP_JIT 映射（内核允许任何被标记为调试的进程使用）。任一种都足够——具体哪种可用取决于设备和 iOS 版本，因此 Husk 会两种都实际测试，而不是直接假定。";

"Husk now runs on iOS 15.5 and later (PS4 games need iOS 17.4)." = "Husk 现在支持 iOS 15.5 及更高版本（PS4 游戏需要 iOS 17.4）。";

"Husk pretends to be a computer on your Wi-Fi, and your %@ pairs with it the way it would with a Mac." = "Husk 会在你的 Wi-Fi 网络中伪装成一台电脑，你的 %@ 会像与 Mac 配对那样与它配对。";

"Husk restores a saved machine instead of booting it, which takes seconds rather than minutes. The picture freezes while it writes. With this off, nothing saves by itself — including after an install." = "Husk 会直接恢复已保存的机器而不是重新启动，只需几秒而不是几分钟。写入期间画面会冻结。关闭此项后不会自动保存任何内容——包括安装之后。";

"Husk runs unmodified Android APKs in a real Android system on your iPhone. The console shows Husk's live log, the guest's serial output and QEMU's own output — the three files any problem here is diagnosed from." = "Husk 会在 iPhone 上的真实安卓系统中运行未经修改的 APK。控制台会显示 Husk 的实时日志、客机的串口输出和 QEMU 自身的输出——这三个文件是诊断此类问题的依据。";

